    {
      "id": "536c0c278b93ba2c5bef",
      "name": "cylindrix",
      "epoch": "0",
      "version": "1.0",
      "release": "49.fc44",
      "architecture": "amd64",
      "summary": "A 3 degrees of freedom combat game",
      "description": "Cylindrix is a 3-on-3 combat game with 360 degrees of freedom that is\nsimilar to Spectre VR but with a wider variety of ships, as well as the\naddition of drivers. Attack and be attacked from all angles as you battle\nin huge orbiting arenas that are each unique in physics, atmospheric\nconditions, and configuration. You must build your team from 37 warriors\nfrom 10 alien races and select from 8 vehicles, each with unique\nmaneuverability, speed, and firepower. The graphics are good, although\nstructure and ship graphics are a little too monotonous. Gameplay is fast\nand furious... so furious, in fact, that it is difficult to differentiate\nbetween friend and foe in the thick of battle. For those who are confident\nof their reflexes or have beaten Spectre and Battlezone, though, this game\nis worth a try.",
      "homepage": "http://www.hardgeus.com/cylindrix/",
      "license": "LGPL-2.0-only",
